task(OMEGA-MARGIN-BINDING-DIAG):
  title    = "report WHICH constraint binds margin_free + revisit H_t danger-face (degen pin)"
  status   = done   // implemented in prior session (2026-07-10): margin_free_binding + margin_entropy + H_T exclusion live in omega_validator.rs
  priority = alta   // gates the Fierro Q1 eps_frontier claim just like OMEGA-MARGIN-DIAG did
  date     = "2026-07-02"
  owner    = "Claude/Fable design ([O]) → DS [S] impl"
  context:
    "OMEGA-MARGIN-DIAG fix is live but margin_free now floors at ~1e-4, bound by a
     continuous dim (very likely normalized H_t/H_rest in the chronic degen phase).
     (1) Add Omega::margin_free_binding(x) -> (name, dist) and emit the binding
         constraint name in kernel_tick so the signal is diagnosable, not opaque.
     (2) Determine if normalized entropy saturates near 1.0 in normal operation
         (read the H_t/H_rest normalization in state_vector.rs / the ingest path). If it
         structurally rests near the Hi face → treat like the categorical gates (danger=Both,
         or a two-band entropy model), else keep Hi (honest degen-proximity signal).
     (3) Consider reporting per-dim margins (not just the min) so one saturated dim does
         not mask early-warning on the others — this is what the Fierro bridge doc needs."
  files    = [projects/vsf-nucleus/src/omega_validator.rs, projects/vsf-nucleus/src/state_vector.rs]
  // ── BINDER CONFIRMED 2026-07-02 (Claude/Fable) → ready [S] spec for DS ────────
  diagnosis_confirmed:
    "Binder = H_T (dim 24). Normalization: state_vector.rs:170 dims[H_T]=h_t/h_max with
     h_max=log2(4)=2.0 (kernel_step.rs:84). Live raw h_t≈2.0 (chronic 'degen' phase) →
     normalized H_T≈1.0 → danger=Hi gives margin=1.0-1.0≈0. So margin_free is floored by a
     STRUCTURALLY SATURATED dim, not a live danger. Two coupled findings:
       (a) margin_free relocation: entropy masks early-warning on all other dims.
       (b) the entropy measure itself saturates — h_t sits at h_max most of the time, so
           the H_t signal is nearly constant/uninformative (alphabet=4 ⇒ h_max=2 bits is
           too small, OR degen is genuinely the operating regime — needs kernel call)."
  design_decision (Fable, for DS to implement):
    "(1) Omega::margin_free_binding(&x) -> (&str, f64); emit omega.margin_binding (name)
         AND omega.margin_free in kernel_tick so the min is never opaque again.
     (2) Re-scale entropy OR change H_T's role in the margin: recommended = keep danger=Hi
         but compute margin_free over the NON-saturated dims and additionally emit
         omega.margin_entropy separately; do NOT let a saturated dim dominate the min the
         Fierro bridge cites. (Equivalent: report per-dim margins, min over 'free' set.)
     (3) Open a separate note on whether h_max=log2(4) undersizes the entropy alphabet —
         that is a kernel-semantics question for rmw3/S5, not part of this [S] impl."
  handoff  = "DS [S]: impl (1)+(2) in omega_validator.rs + operational.rs emit; build 108;
              deploy 101 (another restart seam expected). Design above is complete — no
              further [O] gate. (3) stays with Fable/rmw3."


