task(S5-PUSH):
  title    = "S5 async push — notify rmw3 when pending_human in algedonic_ledger"
  status   = done   // 2026-07-31 channel B (ntfy) LIVE — see S5-PUSH-IMPLEMENTATION below
  priority = baja
  date     = "2026-06-28"
  context:
    "pending_human entries in algedonic_ledger can wait indefinitely if rmw3 is offline.
     Seed: add push notification (email/signal/webhook) when ledger has unack'd entries.
     Ref: seed(S5-PUSH) in MASTER_PLAN ITEM_16."
  gating   = "DONE — ITEM_16 S5 ledger complete (2026-07-26)"
  // ── S5-PUSH-DISPATCH (2026-07-31, Claude): propose 1-2 channels with cost BEFORE code ──
  // DS investigation (2026-07-31): ledger = /root/algedonic/ledger.db on LXC 104
  // (NOT /var/lib/vsf/ledger.db — that file exists but is EMPTY). Table
  // algedonic_ledger, 17 cols (ts, source, type, severity, payload, status
  // default 'pending_human', ack_ts, ack_note, fingerprint, dup_count, first_ts).
  // Current load: 693 pending_human — severity distribution:
  //   sev 10.0 → 74  (merkle_break — content tamper, real; fingerprints empty
  //                    on sev=10 rows — dedupe cannot work on those)
  //   sev  8.0 → 112 | sev 6.0 → 10 | sev 5.0 → 6 | sev 4.0 → 19
  //   sev  2.0 → 138 | sev 0.0 → 334
  // Duplicates: max dup_count = 609, 4449 rows have dup_count > 0 ⇒ a raw
  // "pending_human exists" poll would spam (the 74 merkle_break are ~75% dup
  // of the same underlying event). Any design MUST dedupe (fingerprint +
  // dup_count) and segment by severity — NOT notify per row.
  // Mail infra on LXC 104: postfix ACTIVE (loopback-only, relayhost EMPTY —
  // no external delivery configured yet); sendmail symlink present. No
  // msmtp/ssmtp. Signal/webhook: nothing installed.
  //
  // OPTION A — postfix relay + email (recommended): extend /etc/postfix/main.cf
  //   with a relayhost (SMTP), then a small systemd timer (e.g. every 15 min)
  //   that polls "pending_human AND ack_ts IS NULL AND severity >= 6 AND
  //   first_ts = ts" (dedupe: only the FIRST occurrence of a fingerprint,
  //   suppress repeats with dup_count > 0), groups by severity, sends ONE
  //   digest email to rmw3. Cost: ~1h (postfix relayhost + creds via drop-in,
  //   poller script ~40 lines, unit+timer). Needs: an SMTP relay + recipient
  //   address from rmw3 (nothing exists today).
  // OPTION B — ntfy.sh webhook: poller (same dedupe/segment logic) POSTs a
  //   single JSON digest to a private ntfy topic (or self-hosted ntfy).
  //   Cost: ~45min (no SMTP config; curl POST only). Needs: a topic key +
  //   whether rmw3 uses the ntfy app/Android/Desktop. If both options land,
  //   email remains the durable archive; ntfy is the immediate ping.
  // NOTE: sev=0 (334 rows) should be EXCLUDED from any notification by
  //   default (they are routine status, not alarms) — make threshold configurable.
  // Next: rmw3 picks A and/or B + provides relay/topic/recipient. DS then
  //   implements (poller + unit + timer + dedupe, per chosen channel).
  //
  // ── rmw3 DECISION (2026-07-31) ──────────────────────────────────────────
  // Domain u2738.org available for the email channel (Option A). rmw3
  // configures the Cloudflare DNS side himself (records at his local
  // ~/Documents/u2738.org.txt, NOT in this repo, NOT for DS/Claude to
  // touch) — MX/SPF/DKIM/DMARC etc. DS's side is postfix relayhost config
  // on LXC 104 + the poller; needs the actual outbound SMTP mechanism
  // clarified with rmw3 (self-hosted mail server for u2738.org vs. a
  // third-party transactional relay like SES/Mailgun/Postmark sending as
  // @u2738.org) before wiring relayhost — don't assume either.
  // Build BOTH A and B: "no necesitamos implementar los dos... pero si
  // dejarlo funcional no implica una complejidad mayor, pueden convivir
  // ambas.. evaluemos en la implementación." Not a hard requirement to
  // ship both — DS's own call during implementation whether coexistence
  // is cheap enough to just do, or whether to land B first and treat A as
  // a fast-follow once the SMTP mechanism is settled.


task(A0-CLASSIFIER-CHAIN-FIX):
  title    = "A0_classifier.py: stop appending into vsf_nucleus's canonical events.jsonl"
  status   = done  // 2026-07-02 deployed to LXC 101 (human-confirmed). Verified live: canary-fail
                   // cycle emitted A0_CAPTURE_SUSPECT + s4_ethics_scan into the sidecar; nucleus
                   // chain received ZERO foreign lines post-deploy (all 10 residual foreign lines
                   // in tmpfs timestamped pre-deploy; they age out of s3-star's 10-event window).
  priority = high
  date     = "2026-07-01"
  deploy_note:
    "Prod finding during deploy: the live classifier was an ORPHAN — systemd unit
     inactive+disabled (unit file dated Jun 21), while a manually-launched process (PID
     1529612, started Jun 26) ran with args that differed from the unit on disk
     (--events /run/vsf tmpfs + --cycle-s 300 vs the unit's /var/lib/vsf + 30). It was
     also undeclared in state.db (invisible to the anti-orphan census). Resolution:
     orphan killed (R4-verified), corrected unit installed (live config + --a0-events-out),
     enabled+started under systemd, declared in state.db components (llm_consumer=1) →
     services row live. Repo unit now mirrors prod reality."
  context:
    "Root-caused 105 sev=10.0 merkle_break findings in the algedonic ledger
     (2026-06-27 → 2026-07-01, ~hourly, 105/105 auto-closed by _clf_merkle_break_early
     with an identical canned note 'early-chain bootstrap artifact — service restart').
     Actual cause: A0_classifier.py (S5 watchdog + S4 ethics scanner, LXC 101) reads
     vsf_nucleus's canonical events.jsonl (fine, read-only) but ALSO appended its own
     A0_CAPTURE_SUSPECT / s4_ethics_scan findings directly into that SAME file, with
     no hash/prev_hash/chain_format_version — breaking the single-writer Merkle chain
     contract every ~5min cycle. The Rust nucleus's own in-memory chain state stays
     internally consistent (skips the foreign lines transparently), but any linear
     verifier (s3-star's merkle.rs spot_check) trips on the interleaved unhashed lines.
     Actual nucleus restarts in the same window: ~7, not 105 — the auto-triage's
     'service restart' explanation was never actually correct."
  fix:
    "New --a0-events-out sidecar path (default /var/lib/vsf/a0_classifier/events.jsonl).
     emit_capture_suspect() + _emit_s4_ethics_scan() now write there instead of
     --events. --events remains read-only input for classification. Verified on LXC 108:
     unit-tested both emit fns directly (Ollama unreachable from sandbox network, so the
     full async S4 path couldn't be exercised end-to-end there) — confirmed sidecar
     receives the events and --events file is byte-identical before/after."
  files    = [scripts/A0_classifier.py, scripts/systemd/vsf-a0-classifier.service,
              scripts/deploy_p3b_a0_classifier.sh]
  next     = "(closed — deployed 2026-07-02; follow-ups tracked in A0-TRIAGE-GUARD-FIX,
              A0-SIDECAR-CONSUMERS, A0-READ-EVENTS-TAIL)"


task(A0-READ-EVENTS-TAIL):
  title    = "A0_classifier.py read_events(): stream the tail instead of loading whole file"
  status   = done  // 2026-07-02-ds-5: tail-seek with CHUNK_SIZE=65536; 11/11 tests pass; deployed LXC 101
  priority = medium
  date     = "2026-07-02"
  gating   = "surfaced during A0-CLASSIFIER-CHAIN-FIX certification (LXC 108 OOM)"
  context:
    "read_events() json-parses EVERY line of --events into a Python list and keeps
     only the last PHI_UP_WINDOW_EVENTS (50). On LXC 108's stale 1.9M-line
     events.jsonl this ballooned to ~1GB RSS and the container OOM-killed the
     process (exit 137) — which is also why deploy_p3b_a0_classifier.sh --sandbox
     can no longer pass as written. Prod (LXC 101) currently reads the tmpfs copy
     (small, truncated per nucleus restart) so it is NOT exposed today, but any
     config pointing --events at the unbounded disk file walks into the same OOM.
     Fix: seek from EOF and parse only the last N lines (bounded memory), then the
     sandbox certification path works again on any file size."
  file     = scripts/A0_classifier.py


