task(A0-TRIAGE-GUARD-FIX):
  title    = "vsf_s5_agent.py _clf_merkle_break_early: guard is a no-op, needs real fix"
  status   = superseded  // 2026-07-02 — absorbed into task(TRIAGE-EVIDENCE-RULE)
                         // as its canonical example; fix there, not here
  priority = medium
  date     = "2026-07-01"
  gating   = "surfaced during task(A0-CLASSIFIER-CHAIN-FIX) investigation"
  context:
    "The 'verify chain intact going forward' guard queries
     payload LIKE '%\"event #%' which matches EVERY merkle_break record (all of them
     contain that substring), not specifically high-index ones as the docstring claims —
     so the guard is almost always vacuously true and the auto-dismiss fires
     unconditionally. It also never checks actual systemd restart history nor the
     offending system_id, so it can't distinguish a real restart artifact from a
     foreign-writer chain break (this incident) or genuine tamper. Needs: (1) real
     high-index filter, (2) cross-check against journalctl/state.db restart timestamps
     before asserting 'service restart', (3) surface system_id from the payload so a
     foreign-writer break is labeled distinctly instead of reusing the restart template."
  file     = projects/vsf-s5-algedonic/vsf_s5_agent.py


