// ─── CLAUDE REVIEW 2026-07-13 — S4-OLLAMA-DECOUPLE-V2 verdicts ───────────────
// DS's L1(cpulimit)+L2(keep_alive 5m)+L2b(A0→1.5b)+L4(timeout) landed: host load
// 7.76→2.28, nucleus NRestarts=0 stable. Two items were claude_review — verdicts:
review_verdicts = {
  L3_watchdog:  "APPROVED as proposed. Move start_watchdog_task from tokio::spawn
    (observability.rs:162) to a dedicated std::thread with loop{sleep 10s;
    sd_notify(WATCHDOG=1)}; raise WatchdogSec 30→60. This makes kernel liveness
    immune to runtime saturation — the correct robustness fix. Build 108, R4.",
  L4_tuning:    "OPTION A — num_predict 150→80 (s4_operational.rs:1192). Inference
    ~110s fits a 120s timeout; better cadence than a 240s timeout, and with L3 the
    long-timeout risk is gone anyway. Set timeout=120s to match. VERIFY 80 tokens
    doesn't truncate useful S4 output (it's advisory + concise — should suffice).",
  model_assign: "OPTION 2 — A0 stays on 1.5b (recurring), 7b reserved on-demand
    (KEEP_ALIVE=5m unloads it). Rationale: 2-core hardware can't sustain recurring
    7b. TRADE-OFF (rmw3 should know): A0 is the ETHICAL classifier — 1.5b reasons
    less subtly than 7b. Acceptable because A0 is ADVISORY (flags for human review,
    R11), the deterministic covenant is the floor, not A0. Document as a known
    degradation; 7b remains available on-demand for hard cases.",
}


