      status just never got updated once the follow-up closed.",
  what: "8 new merkle_break sev=10.0 escalations fired 2026-07-27 06:54-14:43 UTC,
      spanning the MERKLE-BREAK-BUFFER-DRIFT fix deploy (07:03 UTC). Signal ids
      4251,4261,4268,4277,4285,4287,4290,4292 (ledger.db, LXC 104). 4251 fired 9min
      BEFORE the fix deploy (old code path). The other 7 all carry the text
      '(CONFIRMED by disk cross-check)' — the new CrossCheckContext logic ran, found
      the buffer mismatch AND the disk copy ALSO mismatches at the same ts. Per the
      fix's own design (merkle.rs verify_chain L192-201) this outcome is classified
      as REAL tamper, not buffer drift — the opposite of what the fix exists to
      filter. Found via onboard.sh at session start; rmw3 explicitly asked to
      investigate with DS before any conclusion.",
  evidence_gate_note: "The evidence-gate's 'Seam signature (event_idx<5)' check
      reports supports=true for all 8, which reads like it corroborates a benign
      chain-restart explanation — it does NOT. merkle.rs verify_chain() enumerate()s
      only the last SAMPLE_N=10 lines read THIS CYCLE (buffer or disk tail), so
      'event #N' in the finding text is a LOCAL index within an arbitrary small
      window, not a position in the real ~521k-line chain. idx<5 fires on roughly
      half of ALL findings by construction, tamper or not — this evidence question
      is not informative and must not be read as seam corroboration. Only the
      restart-window and deploy-window checks (both supports=false for all 8) are
      real evidence here, and both say 'no known event explains this.'",
  ruled_out_so_far: "deploys table (state.db) checked for LXC 101/107: nucleus
      (092dc465..) deployed 2026-07-26 07:16, unchanged since — NOT rebuilt today.
      canonical_hash.rs/event.rs (the shared vsf-agent hash logic both sides use)
      last touched 2026-05-30 / 2026-06-24 — untouched by today's fix, so the hash
      SOURCE code is identical to what wrote these events. BUT two gaps found:
      (a) today's s3-star deploy (fix, live sha f5409597..) has NO row in the
      deploys table (last recorded s3-star deploy is 66afcbc8 on 07-26) — deploy-
      tracking hygiene gap, fix alongside; (b) nucleus (101) DID restart once today
      at 13:27:25 UTC (services_mirror active_since jumped) with no deploys-table
      row either — same sha (092dc465), so a bounce/crash not a redeploy, cause
      unexplained.",
  resolution: "ROOT CAUSE IDENTIFIED — all 8 events are FALSE POSITIVES caused by
      serde_json version skew between the two binaries' shared vsf-agent hash
