task("LXC104-MISSING-NESTING-S5-LATENT-RISK", priority=P1, agent=open, status=complete_2026_08_04) = {
  what: "CRITICAL, confirmed live 2026-08-03 during the fleet-wide sweep
      (task #28, triggered by rmw3 observing elevated PSI/IO-delay in the
      Proxmox panel -- correctly rejected as disk-substrate contention,
      this is a DISTINCT architectural bug). LXC 104 (s5-policy) is the
      ONLY one of the 8 currently-running LXCs (101/104/106/107/108/109/
      110/117) missing `features: nesting=1` in its Proxmox config -- all
      7 others have it. Without nesting, systemd units using mount-
      namespace sandboxing directives (ProtectSystem=strict/full,
      PrivateTmp, etc.) fail at the NAMESPACE step with 'Permission
      denied'.",
  confirmed_broken: [
    "networking.service / systemd-networkd.service / ifupdown-wait-
        online.service / systemd-networkd.socket -- failing since at
        least 2026-07-26 (earliest retained log; true onset may be
        older). Network functionally fine ANYWAY (eth0/eth1 both up,
        Proxmox's own hook-scripts bring up the veth interfaces
        independent of systemd-networkd) -- low real risk, but 8+ days of
        unaddressed failed-unit clutter.",
    "logrotate.service -- failing EVERY DAY since 2026-08-01 (same
        NAMESPACE error). Real risk: unrotated logs, same failure CLASS
        as ALGEDONIC-STORAGE-BLINDSPOT (disk fill from unmanaged growth).",
    "vsf-autoimmune.service -- failed 2026-08-03T19:02:38Z ('start
        operation timed out', 5m6s after start; unit has
        TimeoutStartSec=420 so the exact timing mechanism is
        [UNCERTAIN], not guessed at, but the unit's own
        ProtectSystem=strict directive is the same namespacing
        requirement as the other failures, near-certainly the same root
        cause). This DIRECTLY CONTRADICTS DS's + Claude's earlier same-
        session verification of AUTOIMMUNE-TEST as 'passing' -- that
        check read status WHILE the service was still 'activating'
        (Result=success/ExecMainStatus=0 are default/interim values for a
        running unit, not evidence of completion) and never re-checked
        the FINAL state. function_inventory.vsm's entry for this function
        needs correcting to test_status=failing.",
  ],
  critical_latent_risk: "4 of LXC 104's 5 core S5 governance services --
      vsf-s5-algedonic, vsf-s5-covenant, vsf-s5-ledger,
      vsf-g6-algedonic-sink -- use ProtectSystem=full (SAME directive
      class). All 4 show systemctl is-active=active RIGHT NOW -- but only
      because they have not been restarted since before this broke.
      systemctl is-active tells you a process is currently running, NOT
      that it could successfully START again. The next deploy, crash, or
      host reboot that requires restarting ANY of these 4 will very
